A||||7||vinnywolfe||engine speed & temperature(v6)||||5||
Z||000000||vinnywolfe||07-31-2000||10:10 PM||||i was wondering, since i'm fairly new to this v6 thing, what is the average operating temperature for the 2.8l?  i'm running at about 200-210F and the fan hardly ever comes on. i'm talking about just driving around town or a quick jaunt down the e-way  (not stuck in traffic for a half an hour).<BR>while i'm on the subject of the highway, what should engine speed be at, oh, about 75-80 mph. i'm spinning about 3500+rpm.  <BR>my engine seems to run strong (just a little fluxuation at idle), i'm just used to a buick with a 3.8l and OD.  in that car, the engine is spinning at about 2200rpm @ 72 mph.<P>just wondering,<BR>vinny<BR> <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Standard||07-31-2000||10:29 PM||||The fan switch turns the fan on at 232 degrees, which is too hot for my liking so I wired in a manual switch to turn the fan on..<BR>Fiero's tend to run hotter, especially in around the town driving, because of the set-up of the radiator.. there isn't much air flow until you get on the freeway, which is why hood scoops are a popular mod.  One thing you can do to cool it down is put in a 180* stat. Helps quite a bit<P>As for engine speed, I'm guessing that you have a 4-speed or auto.  My 5 speed is turning a tad under 2,000 at 55 and about 2500 around 75-80.<P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 148,000 miles and counting!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||2birds||07-31-2000||11:00 PM||||Unless I'm in stop and go traffic, which is not that often, mine sits around 165 by the factory temp meter, in town or on the highway, and about 5 degrees lower in the winter.  In the 12 years I've owned it, I've lived in VA, MN, WA, CT and GA, and it has never been any different.  I run the factory 195 degree thermostat.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||86SE||08-01-2000||02:06 AM||||70 MPH=3000 RPM......Auto<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero||||reg||11
Z||000004||86SE||08-01-2000||02:42 AM||||90MPH=4000 RPM, everything past that is a blur.<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||08-01-2000||08:18 AM||||My 85se V-6 4spd runs around 3100 rpms at 70 mph.  I believe the five speeds run around 2200 rpms at 70 mph.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula||08-01-2000||10:06 AM||||Im guessing you dont really have the 5 speed auto or the twin turbo setup? oh well, maybe someone else will come along that has one.  my car runs around 3 grand at 70 and stays around 200 degrees in traffic.||||reg||1
Z||000007||vinnywolfe||08-01-2000||12:33 PM||||thanks guys,  sounds like i'm right in the ballpark.<BR>as far as putting in 180 degree stat,  you probably have to put in a low temp fan switch ALSO, right.  <BR>not to sure those stats and fan switches are any better for the engine.  i think that as long as your around 200F, it's probably better for the engine to run a LITTLE hotter that 165-180.  after all, that's the temperature the car was designed to run at, right?<P>thanks again,<BR>vinny<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||10
